A 65-year-old man presented to the accident and emergency unit with sudden-onset headache, nausea, and vomiting. On examination, he was drowsy with features of third, fourth, and sixth cranial nerve palsy. Urgent MRI of the brain was arranged (see Fig. 1.2).

